<section class="section" id="datasets">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Datasets</span>
      <h2>Datasets</h2>
      <p>Original data built for my research, released openly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ds">
      <article class="dataset">
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/ranjitlall/wingo">World of International Non-Governmental Organizations (WINGO)</a></h3>
        <p>A comprehensive catalogue of formal international non-governmental organizations,
          covering more than 2,600 bodies. Based primarily on the Yearbook of International
          Organizations, with original data on founding and dissolution dates, headquarters
          locations, and issue areas.</p>
        <div class="dataset__meta">
          <a class="btn btn--sm btn--outline" href="https://github.com/ranjitlall/wingo">GitHub &rarr;</a>
          <span class="card__use" style="border:0;padding:0;margin:0">Used in <a href="https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/ajps.12824">&ldquo;Making Global Governance Accountable&rdquo;</a>, <em>AJPS</em> 2025</span>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="dataset">
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/ranjitlall/agg">Accountability in Global Governance (AGG)</a></h3>
        <p>The strength of formal accountability mechanisms in 52 major international
          institutions between 1960 and 2018, across five categories: transparency, evaluation,
          redress, investigation, and participation. Includes governance tasks, decision-making
          procedures, financial resources, and media coverage.</p>
        <div class="dataset__meta">
          <a class="btn btn--sm btn--outline" href="https://github.com/ranjitlall/agg">GitHub &rarr;</a>
          <span class="card__use" style="border:0;padding:0;margin:0">Used in <a href="https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/ajps.12824">&ldquo;Making Global Governance Accountable&rdquo;</a>, <em>AJPS</em> 2025</span>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="dataset">
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/ranjitlall/piip">Performance of International Institutions Project (PIIP)</a></h3>
        <p>Performance assessments of 54 major institutions between 2008 and 2018, produced by
          the governments of Australia, Denmark, the Netherlands, Sweden, and the United
          Kingdom, and by the Multilateral Organisation Performance Assessment Network (MOPAN).
          Also covers policy autonomy, governance tasks, and operational partnerships.</p>
        <div class="dataset__meta">
          <a class="btn btn--sm btn--outline" href="https://github.com/ranjitlall/piip">GitHub &rarr;</a>
          <span class="card__use" style="border:0;padding:0;margin:0">Used in <a href="https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/making-international-institutions-work/2B354270D50B9471D04529CD8D5C98F7"><em>Making International Institutions Work</em></a>, CUP 2023</span>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="dataset">
        <h3><a href="https://www.aiddata.org/data/project-performance-database-ppd-version-2-0">Project Performance Database (PPD) 2.1</a></h3>
        <p>The world&rsquo;s largest dataset of international development projects with
          quantitative measures of overall performance: evaluations of more than 20,000 foreign
          aid projects in 183 countries between 1956 and 2016, by 12 bilateral and multilateral
          agencies. Developed with Dan Honig and Bradley Parks.</p>
        <div class="dataset__meta">
          <a class="btn btn--sm btn--outline" href="https://www.aiddata.org/data/project-performance-database-ppd-version-2-0">AidData &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="dataset">
        <h3><a href="https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataverse/harvard/?q=ranjit+lall">Replication data</a></h3>
        <p>Data and code for my other published research are available through the Harvard
          Dataverse.</p>
        <div class="dataset__meta">
          <a class="btn btn--sm btn--outline" href="https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataverse/harvard/?q=ranjit+lall">Dataverse &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="software">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Software</span>
      <h2>Software</h2>
      <p>Open-source packages for missing-data analysis using machine learning.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="suite">
      <img src="{{ '/assets/img/midasverse.png' | url }}" alt="" width="150" height="150">
      <div>
        <p><strong>MIDASverse</strong> is a suite of Python and R packages for missing-data
          analysis using machine learning, developed with Thomas Robinson. Introduced in
          <a href="https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/political-analysis/article/abs/midas-touch-accurate-and-scalable-missingdata-imputation-with-deep-learning/5007854F57E88AF16D69BCCA4C5AF1FF">&ldquo;The MIDAS Touch&rdquo;</a>, <em>Political Analysis</em> 2022, and
          <a href="https://www.jstatsoft.org/article/view/v107i09">&ldquo;Efficient Multiple Imputation&rdquo;</a>, <em>JSS</em> 2023.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pkg">
      <div class="pkgrow">
        <span class="pkgrow__n"><a href="https://github.com/MIDASverse/MIDASpy">MIDASpy</a></span>
        <span class="pkgrow__lang">Python &middot; PyPI</span>
        <span class="pkgrow__d">Accurate and efficient multiple imputation with deep learning.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pkgrow">
        <span class="pkgrow__n"><a href="https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/rMIDAS/index.html">rMIDAS</a></span>
        <span class="pkgrow__lang">R &middot; CRAN</span>
        <span class="pkgrow__d">R equivalent of MIDASpy.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pkgrow">
        <span class="pkgrow__n"><a href="https://github.com/MIDASverse/citest">citest</a></span>
        <span class="pkgrow__lang">Python &middot; PyPI</span>
        <span class="pkgrow__d">Tests conditional independence in incomplete regression analysis with machine learning.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pkgrow">
        <span class="pkgrow__n"><a href="https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/citestR/index.html">citestR</a></span>
        <span class="pkgrow__lang">R &middot; CRAN</span>
        <span class="pkgrow__d">R equivalent of citest.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

